team":"LA","distance":0.4159,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Raheem Morris"},{"season":2022,"team":"MIN","distance":0.4307,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"IND","distance":0.4441,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.456,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Eagles are 2-7 through week 9 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 221 to 148. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 30th in EPA per play and the defense 29th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits are the 2nd highest no-huddle rate and the fewest defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Eagles offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest no-huddle rate and a shotgun rate that was among the highest in the league. Jalen Hurts has run the passing game, with Makai Lemon leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Eagles have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, success rate allowed, only ranks 17th, and it is 32nd in takeaways per game. Jalen Carter has led the way with 5 sacks. Schematically, they have the fewest defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Eagles have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 60% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 88% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Jalen Hurts has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 933 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Makai Lemon and Dallas Goedert leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Saquon Barkley and Dameon Pierce. On defense, Jalen Carter leads the team with 5 sacks.","coaching":"Sean Mannion is calling the offense and Vic Fangio is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Saints under Kellen Moore and the 2022 Colts under Frank Reich. Their defense looks most like the 2025 49ers under Robert Saleh and the 2023 Rams under Raheem Morris.","trends":"The offense went from 15th in EPA per play in 2025 to 30th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 8th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 26% to 60%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}